ps://t.co/OHZlthmVyy https://t.co/Vf28vyXCWx", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2114394052057837578"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-25T16:00:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114386674964963735"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Emerging markets’ growing economic clout is not matched by their influence in global governance", "display_url": "imf.org/en/publication…", "end": 185, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/fandd/issues/2026/09/book-review-the-rise-of-emerged-markets-mahmood-pradhan", "images": [{"height": 1077, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114386718354964480/Uw8YL5GF?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2656}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114386718354964480/Uw8YL5GF?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 162, "status": 200, "title": "The Rise of ‘Emerged’ Markets", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/fandd/issues/2026/09/book-review-the-rise-of-emerged-markets-mahmood-pradhan", "url": "https://t.co/SbPd8JiYQS"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/EbAAdnNNGf", "end": 209, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114386674964963735/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114386542122913792", "start": 186, "url": "https://t.co/EbAAdnNNGf"}]}, "id": "2114386674964963735", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 13234, "like_count": 36, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Are emerging markets still “emerging”? Mahmood Pradhan reviews a new book that argues many have already transformed their economic prospects in F&amp;D magazine. https://t.co/SbPd8JiYQS https://t.co/EbAAdnNNGf", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114386674964963735"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-25T15:30:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114378960553599017"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Diversification strengthens resilience, but it requires connectivit...", "display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=Mmlx-8…", "end": 239, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mmlx-8iveXY", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114378965762949120/iv1ONkO5?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114378965762949120/iv1ONkO5?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 216, "status": 200, "title": "Analytical Corner: Mind the Gaps---Caribbean Trade Patterns and the Connectivity Constraints", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mmlx-8iveXY", "url": "https://t.co/qGpGFYsIKU"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/ghRMJT02X6", "end": 263, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114378960553599017/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114378957898571776", "start": 240, "url": "https://t.co/ghRMJT02X6"}]}, "id": "2114378960553599017", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 12933, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Limited shipping and air links constrain trade and tourism diversification in the Caribbean, leaving economies exposed to shocks. In this Analytical Corner, JaeBin Ahn explains why connectivity is key to resilience: https://t.co/qGpGFYsIKU https://t.co/ghRMJT02X6", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114378960553599017"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-25T13:07:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114343215520244108"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 196, "id": "1260941", "start": 192, "username": "imf"}, {"end": 214, "id": "88744839", "start": 208, "username": "gmaol"}], "urls": [{"description": "Sign up for the free Econvitals email briefings: a Morning Note, a Daily Economic Briefing, weekly and monthly briefings, data-release emails and the noon Reaction and Roundup. Confirmed opt-in, cancel any time.", "display_url": "econvitals.org/subscribe/", "end": 287, "expanded_url": "https://econvitals.org/subscribe/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113673096334839808/cxAG0dYq?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113673096334839808/cxAG0dYq?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 264, "status": 200, "title": "Sign up — Econvitals", "unwound_url": "https://econvitals.org/subscribe/", "url": "https://t.co/NM6bWOgK2b"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/EhEmjcZzm8", "end": 311, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114343215520244108/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114341002760667137", "start": 288, "url": "https://t.co/EhEmjcZzm8"}]}, "id": "2114343215520244108", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 8904, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Thousands signed up for Econvitals! But some tried &amp; failed. If you're one:\n\n1. Try again, an overactive anti-bot filter was rejecting some, it's been fixed\n\n2. Type correctly. (e.g., the @imf.orgp &amp; @gmaol.com  who tried)\n\n3. Check spam for confirmation\n\nhttps://t.co/NM6bWOgK2b https://t.co/EhEmjcZzm8", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114343215520244108"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-25T13:00:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114341323994284259"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The latest World Economic Outlook highlights widening growth divergences, renewed inflation pressures, and mounting downside risks. Fiscal space needs to be urgently rebuilt. Governments should favor targeted support over price controls and recognize the trade-offs involving corporate income tax policy.", "display_url": "imf.org/en/publication…", "end": 257, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/weo/issues/2026/10/13/world-economic-outlook-october-2026?cid=sm-com-x-am26-WEOEA20206002", "images": [{"height": 350, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114341265538162688/XN_y6wbk?format=png&name=orig", "width": 600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114341265538162688/XN_y6wbk?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 234, "status": 200, "title": "World Economic Outlook, October 2026: Resilience Under Strain, Urgent Choices", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/weo/issues/2026/10/13/world-economic-outlook-october-2026?cid=sm-com-x-am26-WEOEA20206002", "url": "https://t.co/vwXHRxkW4n"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/RfkgKfbfQy", "end": 281, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114341323994284259/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114341218939498496", "start": 258, "url": "https://t.co/RfkgKfbfQy"}]}, "id": "2114341323994284259", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 22, "impression_count": 21072, "like_count": 147, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 53}, "text": "Cost-of-living crises hit lower-income households hardest. Governments often rely on broad subsidies and tax cuts, but new IMF research finds targeted and temporary transfers best protect the vulnerable while preserving fiscal space.\nhttps://t.co/vwXHRxkW4n https://t.co/RfkgKfbfQy", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114341323994284259"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-25T12:44:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114337256865493250"], "id": "2114337256865493250", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 228, "impression_count": 92248, "like_count": 720, "quote_count": 25, "reply_count": 312, "retweet_count": 34}, "text": "A thing I see happening at large organizations as a result of AI is the expansion of the role and span of control of senior management who can directly monitor the whole firm. It vastly changes company operations. It also is straightforward to implement compared to firm redesign.", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2114337256865493250"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-25T00:01:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114145384318591143"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/econvitals/sta…", "end": 247, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/econvitals/status/2114034657465450913", "start": 224, "url": "https://t.co/ZzL9rBThNv"}]}, "id": "2114145384318591143", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 11114, "like_count": 41, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 7}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114034657465450913", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "A way to summarize and aggregate the latest data flow. Two dimensions:\n\n(1) How is the data relative to what happened in the past? How is it compared to what was expected the day before release?\n\n(2) Activity and inflation. https://t.co/ZzL9rBThNv", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114145384318591143"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T22:41:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114125216180039906"], "id": "2114125216180039906", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 7831, "like_count": 26, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Why is Argon not available in Antigravity 🤔", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114125216180039906"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T21:32:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114107760480755899"], "id": "2114107760480755899", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2660, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Diet Coke ICEEs would heal America", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114107760480755899"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:30:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114092125080146143"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qNJDx7vioK", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114092125080146143/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114092072550670336", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/qNJDx7vioK"}]}, "id": "2114092125080146143", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 21078, "like_count": 44, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "1/3 Growth in Latin America and the Caribbean remains resilient, projected at 2.3% in 2026, 2.5% in 2027, and 2.9% in 2028. Strong U.S. demand, high commodity prices, favorable financial conditions, tourism, and remittances are offsetting trade and geopolitical pressures. https://t.co/qNJDx7vioK", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114092125080146143"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-24T19:06:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114071006633501034"], "id": "2114071006633501034", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 38785, "like_count": 246, "quote_count": 16, "reply_count": 44, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "Markets continued to revisit this past week the previously comforting assumptions around tech ROI and funding needs, triggering NASDAQ market weakness and a flight to quality, even as confidence in the sector’s long-term economic growth effects remains broadly intact.\nLooking", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114071006633501034"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:30:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114046770531663926"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "What happens when grocery and utility bills soar? This talk explore...", "display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH…", "end": 230, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH7KvWY", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113729750674145280/C6ZatK0m?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113729750674145280/C6ZatK0m?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 207, "status": 200, "title": "Analytical Corner: Navigating a Shock-Prone World: Lessons from Cost-of-Living Crises", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mWvNmH7KvWY", "url": "https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Pr7IjqbkMK", "end": 254, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114046770531663926/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114046768258359297", "start": 231, "url": "https://t.co/Pr7IjqbkMK"}]}, "id": "2114046770531663926", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 20978, "like_count": 95, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 22}, "text": "When grocery and utility bills soar, the burden is not shared equally. This Analytical Corner explores who is most affected, why the distributional consequences matter, and how policy can make a difference: https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI https://t.co/Pr7IjqbkMK", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2114046770531663926"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:13:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114042558074806389"], "id": "2114042558074806389", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2453, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Don't abliterate and drive", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114042558074806389"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:41:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114034453131764202"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/x0S3eJFCCl", "end": 90, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114034453131764202/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114030311554052097", "start": 67, "url": "https://t.co/x0S3eJFCCl"}]}, "id": "2114034453131764202", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 19368, "like_count": 96, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "A college student reacts to some of what is written by Econvitals. https://t.co/x0S3eJFCCl", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114034453131764202"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:33:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114032505305354626"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 149, "start": 145, "tag": "qpr"}], "mentions": [{"end": 154, "id": "71210107", "start": 150, "username": "QPR"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/VwXoAr7XSx", "end": 178, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114032505305354626/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114032500313915392", "start": 155, "url": "https://t.co/VwXoAr7XSx"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/VwXoAr7XSx", "end": 178, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114032505305354626/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114032500280266752", "start": 155, "url": "https://t.co/VwXoAr7XSx"}]}, "id": "2114032505305354626", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 32213, "like_count": 170, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "A decisive win like this doesn’t happen often for QPR—or any team I support, for that matter. \nI'm currently alternating between shock and joy! \n#qpr @QPR https://t.co/VwXoAr7XSx", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114032505305354626"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114031666587168877"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 32, "start": 24, "tag": "BLSdata"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Bureau of Labor Statistics is the principal fact-finding agency for the Federal Government in the broad field of labor economics and statistics.", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/update.htm", "end": 98, "expanded_url": "https://bls.gov/opub/update.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111846596279402496/98Bnf4uL?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111846596279402496/98Bnf4uL?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 75, "status": 200, "title": "U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/", "url": "https://t.co/6g1gI94GS0"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/wdThC30hcH", "end": 122, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2114031666587168877/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113655574122438656", "start": 99, "url": "https://t.co/wdThC30hcH"}]}, "id": "2114031666587168877", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2797, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Catch up on all the new #BLSdata and publications that came out this week! https://t.co/6g1gI94GS0 https://t.co/wdThC30hcH", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2114031666587168877"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:10:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114026870098518060"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/AISecurityInst…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AISecurityInst/status/2113626762617741389?s=20", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/FCIpX5tdUR"}]}, "id": "2114026870098518060", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 3343, "like_count": 47, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113626762617741389", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I'm glad Ant and AISI dug deeper here, though for the record, it already seemed in July like Anthropic's defense of Mythos's behavior was rushed + that motivated reasoning was prob at work\n\nAlso, Astra being v. bad here too is an important finding as well https://t.co/FCIpX5tdUR", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114026870098518060"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:38:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114003560723534156"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A note from the site's launch: what a company would have needed to build Econvitals with every line of code written by people.", "display_url": "econvitals.org/about/before-a…", "end": 246, "expanded_url": "https://econvitals.org/about/before-ai/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114003562518781952/_nAeYfCI?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114003562518781952/_nAeYfCI?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 223, "status": 200, "title": "What would it have taken to build Econvitals before AI? — Econvitals", "unwound_url": "https://econvitals.org/about/before-ai/", "url": "https://t.co/eu9k5HxEHo"}]}, "id": "2114003560723534156", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 97, "impression_count": 62576, "like_count": 206, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 32, "retweet_count": 19}, "text": "I asked Claude how much it would have taken to develop Econvitals pre-coding agents. It's answer: a team of about 50 people working for three years with a budget of $20 million.\n\nIs this correct or too high? I'm not sure.\n\nhttps://t.co/eu9k5HxEHo", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114003560723534156"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:30:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114001653879672877"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 223, "id": "825088493764407298", "start": 211, "username": "polynoamial"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/andrewcurran_/…", "end": 307, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/andrewcurran_/status/2113717691420950973", "start": 284, "url": "https://t.co/jJiU7pV2iv"}]}, "id": "2114001653879672877", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 80, "impression_count": 37963, "like_count": 468, "quote_count": 21, "reply_count": 215, "retweet_count": 49}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113717691420950973", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Without being overly credulous, we should be taking seemingly “out there” ideas about AI cybersecurity from the Labs more seriously. Examples: Anthropic was mocked for saying Mythos-level AI changed cyber &amp; @polynoamial for saying that models would find novel ways to coordinate. https://t.co/jJiU7pV2iv", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2114001653879672877"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:19:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113998856669016457"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 37, "id": "2592325153", "start": 24, "username": "Claudia_Sahm"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Claudia_Sahm/s…", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Claudia_Sahm/status/2113948073671921972", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/lM3dcySv7G"}]}, "id": "2113998856669016457", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 59, "impression_count": 41543, "like_count": 173, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 14}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113948073671921972", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I mostly agree with you @Claudia_Sahm.\n\nI expect colleagues to continue to have research assistants even if only for mentorship than because they need the help.\n\nCompanies to have junior staff not because they need their current work but to train them for future roles. https://t.co/lM3dcySv7G", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113998856669016457"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "332617373", "name": "Mohamed A. El-Erian", "username": "elerianm"}, {"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "612896910", "name": "BLS-Labor Statistics", "username": "BLS_gov"}, {"id": "25098482", "name": "IMF", "username": "IMFNews"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "1214528593", "name": "Miles Brundage", "username": "Miles_Brundage"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2114406141711032698", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlwu1v8mhtqao4q8dxjdmizwfibh", "oldest_id": "2113998856669016457", "result_count": 23}}
